course: dictionary
lesson: 4383
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as 1), 2), 3) and so on. To pick the right one, read the words around it, which is its context. «Ella's account had been hacked, and the hacker was asking everyone on her list.» The clues are account and hacked, so a hacker here is a person who gets into a computer system without permission.
explain: The same word can also mean something clever and playful. «Hacker» once meant a skilled programmer who enjoys solving computer problems in clever ways. A puzzle-loving programmer and a criminal who steals data are very different people, so the clue words tell you which meaning to pick.
explain: Some hackers are paid to help. «Ethical hackers are hired with written permission to test systems and report weaknesses.» The words ethical, hired and permission show this hacker is on the good side, and the permission is what makes the work legal.
explain: Always check your choice. Swap the meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If it does not, try the next meaning in the dictionary.
fact: A hacker is a person who uses computer skills to get into computers or systems, often without permission, which is a crime.
fact: A hacker can also be a very skilled programmer who enjoys solving computer problems in clever ways.
fact: An ethical hacker, also called a white-hat hacker, is paid to find weak spots so they can be fixed.
fact: In the news, «hackers stole data» means criminals got into a computer system.
fact: In sport, informal slang, a hacker is a poor player, especially in golf.
exercise: «Ella's account had been hacked, and the hacker was asking everyone on her list.» What does hacker mean here? | Someone who fixes broken roads | A poor golf player | A very skilled programmer who loves puzzles | *A person who gets into a system without permission
exercise: «Ethical hackers are hired with written permission to test systems.» Why is an ethical hacker's work legal? | *They have permission to do it | They break rules for fun | They never report what they find | They work in secret, at night
exercise: Sam says, «He's a real hacker on the course, he never hits the green.» What does hacker mean in this sentence? | A person who builds bridges | A clever programmer | A criminal who steals data | *A poor player, especially in golf
test: «Hackers stole data from the company last night.» Which word is the clue that the hacker is a criminal? | company | night | *stole | last
test: «Hacker» once meant a clever, playful programmer. What did the word first mean? | A poor golfer | *A clever, playful programmer | A criminal who steals data | A person who fixes roads
exam: Which is the best way to find the right meaning of a word with several meanings? | *Read the sentence around it and try each meaning in place of the word | Skip the sentence and copy the dictionary | Ask the loudest person in the class | Guess the first meaning and never check it
